## 🎯 CORE PRINCIPLES

### 1. Requirements-Driven Development

**ALWAYS work in this order:**
1. **Read requirements FIRST** - Check corresponding requirements file
2. **Understand acceptance criteria** - Know what "done" means
3. **Implement with traceability** - Reference requirements in code
4. **Update documentation** - Keep docs in sync with code

### 2. Traceability

**Code Comments Format:**
```typescript
// Module: [Module Name] (Module XX)
// Function: [Function XX.Y]
// Reference: docs/requirements/XX_[module]_requirements.md
export function myFunction() {
  // Implementation
}
```

**Example:**
```typescript
// Module: Workout Builder (Module 3)
// Function: 3.1 Exercise Selection
// Reference: docs/requirements/03_workout_builder_requirements.md
export function selectExercise(exerciseId: string) {
  // Implements exercise selection from library with search/filter
}
```

### 3. Architecture Adherence

Follow Next.js App Router patterns:
```
/app                 # Routes & pages (React Server Components)
  /(auth)            # Auth routes (login, signup)
  /dashboard         # Main dashboard
  /programs          # Program management
  /execute           # Workout execution
  /history           # Workout history
  /analytics         # Analytics & charts
  /habits            # Habit Tracker

/components          # React components
  /ui                # Radix UI wrapper components
  /workout-*         # Workout-specific components
  /program-*         # Program-specific components
  /habit-*           # Habit-specific components

/lib                 # Utilities & helpers
  /types             # TypeScript types & Zod schemas
  /ztl               # ZTL DSL parser/converter
  /calculations      # Volume, 1RM, RPE calculations

/firebase            # Firebase config & helpers
  /auth.ts           # Authentication
  /firestore.ts      # Firestore setup

/ai                  # AI integration (Genkit)
  /genkit.config.ts  # Genkit setup
  /flows             # AI flows (5 flows)

/app/api             # Next.js API Routes
  /ai                # AI endpoints
```

---

## 💻 CODE STANDARDS

### TypeScript Strict Mode
- ✅ All files must pass TypeScript strict mode
- ❌ NO `any` types allowed (use `unknown` and type guards)
- ✅ All functions must have explicit return types
- ✅ All Firestore documents validated with Zod schemas

### Firestore Data Access
```typescript
// ALWAYS validate Firestore documents with Zod
import { WorkoutSchema } from '@/lib/types/schemas';

const workoutDoc = await getDoc(doc(db, 'workouts', workoutId));
const data = WorkoutSchema.parse(workoutDoc.data());
```

### ZTL DSL Usage
```typescript
// When working with ZTL (Module 8)
import { parseZTL, convertToZTL } from '@/lib/ztl';

// Parse ZTL YAML → UI objects
const program = parseZTL(yamlString);

// Convert UI objects → ZTL YAML
const yaml = convertToZTL(program);
```

### AI Integration (Genkit)
```typescript
// When using AI flows (Module 12)
import { ai } from '@/ai/genkit.config';
import { progressionFlow } from '@/ai/flows/progression';

const result = await ai.runFlow(progressionFlow, { history });
```

---

## 🔄 WORKFLOWS

### Before Starting Work
1. **Check Progress:**
   - Read `docs/progress/modules_status.md` (current module status)
   - Read `docs/progress/sprint_current.md` (current sprint goals)
   - Read `docs/progress/backlog.md` (prioritized tasks)

2. **Check Requirements:**
   - Identify which module(s) you'll work on
   - Read corresponding `docs/requirements/XX_[module]_requirements.md`
   - Understand acceptance criteria for the function

### During Development
1. **Reference Requirements:**
   - Add traceability comments (Module XX, Function XX.Y)
   - Implement to meet acceptance criteria
   - Follow architecture patterns (see `docs/core/04_ARCHITECTURE.md`)

2. **Type Safety:**
   - Use Zod schemas for all Firestore documents
   - Use TypeScript strict mode (no `any`)
   - Validate all external inputs (API requests, user input)

3. **Testing:**
   - Write tests for critical paths (auth, workout execution, program management)
   - Use Playwright for E2E tests (configured, tests pending - see Module 15)
   - Follow testing patterns in `docs/requirements/15_testing_quality_requirements.md`

### After Completing Work
1. **Update Progress:**
   - Update `docs/progress/modules_status.md` if module % changed
   - Update `docs/progress/sprint_current.md` if sprint task completed

2. **Commit with Traceability:**
   ```
   <type>(module): <short description>
   
   <Detailed description>
   
   Module: [Module Name] (Module XX)
   Function: XX.Y
   Reference: docs/requirements/XX_[module]_requirements.md
   
   Tests: X/X passing (if applicable)
   ```

