## ⚠️ CRITICAL RULES

### NEVER
- ❌ Write code without reading requirements first
- ❌ Use `any` type (TypeScript strict mode enforced)
- ❌ Write to Firestore without Zod validation
- ❌ Commit without traceability comments
- ❌ Skip tests for critical paths (auth, execution, data persistence)

### ALWAYS
- ✅ Read requirements FIRST (`docs/requirements/XX_[module]_requirements.md`)
- ✅ Add traceability comments (Module XX, Function XX.Y)
- ✅ Validate Firestore data with Zod schemas
- ✅ Update progress files after completing tasks
- ✅ Test critical user flows (E2E recommended - see Module 15)

